From c35a22e455ac15feb23568cded22b48f7c6cc7c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: fence regulatory submissions after terminal
 join close

Explicit stop closes the join lifetime before dropping the mac mutex for
worker cancellation. A regulatory callback can run during that gap or
after stop. When cleanup_done is true, the existing healthy regulatory
restore exception returns false from join_regulatory_stop, so the notifier
continues to submit domain and power commands despite join_closed.

Check the terminal fence in the actual notifier under the existing mutex,
before the benign-retirement exception. Healthy two-lifetime rearm leaves
join_closed clear and retains its regulatory restore behavior. Do not
clear poison, alter command/page ownership, lift a budget or add an IRQ
operation.

Host tests compile the actual stop, close, regulatory admission and sender
bodies with kernel/policy/HIF-boundary shims. The old source submits in the
close/cancel gap; the fixed source refuses before any sender or debit.
These tests do not prove kernel concurrency or firmware behavior.

Internal experiment archive, not submission-ready; no DCO certification.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index d30c30f..c592f55 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -347,6 +347,8 @@ static void mt6797_mac_regulatory(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 	if (mac->closing || mac->first_error)
 		goto out;
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MT6797_STATION_JOIN)
+	if (mac->join_closed)
+		goto out;
 	if (mt6797_mac_join_regulatory_stop(mac, &discard, &internal))
 		goto out;
 #endif
